    "_style": "Friendly modern everyday Malayalam in Malayalam script (reformed script with chillu letters ൽ ൻ ർ ൾ ൺ, as on phones), polite നിങ്ങൾ; present and imperative forms keep it gender-neutral, keep third person neutral. Neither stiff Sanskritised coinages nor heavy English transliteration: common Malayalam app words (ക്രമീകരണം, തിരയുക, പങ്കിടുക, അറിയിപ്പ്), loanwords people really say (പോസ്റ്റ്, ചാറ്റ്, പ്രൊഫൈൽ, ലൈവ്, ഗെയിം, ആപ്പ്, ലിങ്ക്). Buttons: short polite -ുക imperative (സേവ് ചെയ്യുക, പങ്കിടുക, കാണുക). Malayalam renders among the longest — always pick the shortest natural label for buttons, tabs, chips, HUD and notification titles (≤ 1.6× English). Western digits. Understandable in Kerala, Lakshadweep and the Gulf/Western diaspora. Brand names stay Latin ({{@…}} tokens); keep AI, OTP, PIN, URL, GIF, DM, QR, Wi-Fi, PDF, ID, FAQ as they are.",
